title: Bars drawn with pictures
intro: A Bar's fill and background can be your own pictures: the fill is revealed as it fills, never squeezed, over a background that stretches like a nine-slice panel.
project: Empty | Bar Images
write: Sprites/gauge.png | bar-images/gauge.png
write: Sprites/frame.png | bar-images/frame.png

chapter: A fill picture | Fill Image
create: Bar
rename: Gauge
set: Transform.Position = 0, 0, 0
set: Bar.Size = 6, 1
set: Bar.Max = 10
set: Bar.Value = 5
look: 0, 0, 2.5
say: Here's a bar, half full, drawn in plain colors as bars always have been.
pickimage: Bar.FillImage = Sprites/gauge.png
explain: field:Bar.FillImage | Fill Image | Give it a Fill Image, picked like any other picture. It's laid over the whole bar and shown only as far as the bar is full.
set: Bar.Fill = #FFFFFF
explain: field:Bar.Fill | Fill tints it | The Fill color tints the picture, as a sprite's Tint does. White shows it as it was painted.
explain: scene | Cut off, not squeezed | Half full shows the left half of the gauge, its tick marks where they'll stay. Nothing is squashed to fit.
set: Bar.Value = 8
say: Fill it more, and more of the same picture shows.
play
expectdrawn: -1.5, 0 = lit
stop

chapter: A framed background | Background Image and Background Slice
pickimage: Bar.BackgroundImage = Sprites/frame.png
set: Bar.Background = #FFFFFF
explain: field:Bar.BackgroundImage | Background Image | The Background Image is drawn whole behind the fill, tinted by the Background color.
say: This frame is a small square picture, so stretched along the bar its border gets thick at the ends.
set: Bar.BackgroundSlice = 0.125
set: Bar.BackgroundSliceSize = 0.125
explain: field:Bar.BackgroundSlice | Background Slice | Background Slice makes it a nine-slice, as a sprite's Slice does: the outer eighth of the picture is border, drawn an eighth of a unit thick, and its corners keep their shape however long the bar is.
set: Bar.Value = 5
play
expectdrawn: -1.5, 0 = lit
expectdrawn: 1.5, 0 = dark
stop

chapter: Any direction | Direction
set: Bar.Direction = Left
explain: field:Bar.Direction | Direction | It fills whichever way its Direction says. Filling from the right, it shows the right half of the gauge.
play
expectdrawn: 1.5, 0 = lit
expectdrawn: -1.5, 0 = dark
stop
say: The game and the web player draw it exactly as the Scene view does. And with no pictures set, a bar is plain colors, just as before.
